\cfg{xhtml-template-filename}{%k.html}

JoliPuTTY is a playful fork of PuTTY, the free (MIT-licensed) Windows
Telnet and SSH client, which gives PuTTY a modern WinUI 3 look on
Windows 11, with tabs, split panes and a redesigned configuration
window. This manual documents JoliPuTTY, and PuTTY's companion
utilities PSCP, PSFTP, Plink, Pageant and PuTTYgen.

\k{joliputty} describes what JoliPuTTY does differently from PuTTY.
The rest of the manual is PuTTY's own: it still says \q{PuTTY}, and
describes PuTTY's configuration dialog box, whose settings JoliPuTTY
keeps, although some of them are on different pages (see
\k{jp-config-moved}).

Like PuTTY's, this manual is about the Windows versions of the
tools. JoliPuTTY doesn't change the \i{Unix version} of PuTTY.

\e{JoliPuTTY is an independent project, and is not affiliated with
the PuTTY project. It is provided as is, without any warranty.}

